OL,3,AChina advises its citizens to leave
OL,4,ATaiwan ally Eswatini over 'security
OL,5,Arisks'
OL,6,
OL,7,FChina's foreign ministry has told its
OL,8,Fcitizens to leave the southern African
OL,9,Fkingdom of Eswatini over "security
OL,10,Frisks".
OL,12,FThe ministry cited "rampant cyber fraud
OL,13,Fand criminal activities associated with
OL,14,Fgambling" as among its security
OL,15,Fconcerns, but did not give details.
OL,17,FIt suggested its citizens relocate as
OL,18,Fsoon as possible to "relatively safer"
OL,19,Fcountries such as neighbouring South
OL,20,FAfrica.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
